title Existence is not coverage -- the Tally caller map read nineteen of sixty-eight
prompt the standing baton -- take the next agent-doable lap in the mantra/ and tally/ lane
rota lap 4160, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears. The threshold's own hard sentence is the one the lap then walked into: a guard that cannot red guards nothing. The grain page beside it seats count, never number, and both readings named the fault before it was found.
think Opened with fleet_round_open on 88790efa2e, already on the anointed order, and a cold scoped roster pass -- 154 guards, 151 green, 0 red, 3 gated, 1138s, tree_moved=no.
think Lane survey first. mantra/ holds 27 flat and 35 recursive files; its weave already publishes merge and annotate, and the one thing its head still names as open -- the several-line interleave wanting an anchor per insert -- is a seam awaiting Keaton's word rather than a lap.
think Turned to tally/. Twenty-seven witnesses stand in tools/t/ and only two rows name tally on the standing roster, which looked like %360's shape in my own lane -- so I measured rather than assumed. unheard_guard_scan named exactly ONE: tools/t/tally_caller_map_witness.rish. Twenty-six are reached transitively by tally_roster. The hypothesis was wrong and the measurement was cheap.
think Read that one guard. tools/fixtures/t/tally_caller_map_scan.sh carried a literal list of nineteen caller paths and ran a single test over each -- does it exist. tally/README.md's canon says a caller reaches a mark through its own symlink into tally/, never through a copy, and 477 living pages cite that front door. Existence answers neither half of that sentence.
think Measured the population the list stands for. Resolving every tracked symlink outside tally/ and asking which land on a tally/ file: 68 carriers across 23 rooms, chains walked (granary/parse_int.rye reaches tally through linengrow). Nine of those rooms appear in no cell of the canon table -- dimeroll, docs-geode, image, kumara, lotus, mandate, mycelium, settlement, vault. Every gap ran one way, under-named.
think Checked for a peer first. copy_lag, seated by another ship 20260906.070240, already reads 108 basenames the tree keeps both ways and already names caravan/parse_int.rye -- a regular file whose own head reads tally/parse_int.rye, drifted from it in two comment lines -- inside a ceiling of 2. So the copy class is gated one room over, and this guard reports it and cites that gate rather than growing a second one.
think Also read the elder copy_sameness guard, which is unheard and whose corpus emptied: it compares every tally_copy.rye against the canon and reads real_files=0, so its drift gate cannot fire. Named on no card this lap; the finding is recorded here and the wider guard already supersedes it.
think Rewrote the scan as a derived census with two gates, each in the direction a real change breaks it: broken, a carrier whose target no longer resolves, which is what the elder list was truly testing; and stale_named, a family the canon table names that carries nothing, which is the mirror -- a list can be wrong in two directions and a guard watching one reports the other as green.
think Refusals before a count: marks_absent when tally/ publishes nothing, table_absent when the canon section leaves the README, hop_bound when a symlink chain outruns its named ceiling of eight. A census that reads nothing and reports nothing wrong is indistinguishable from a healthy tree.
think A copy is found by its head rather than by its name. Basenames collide honestly -- aurora/src/seed.rye, brushstroke/seed.rye, caravan/seed.rye and lotus/stack.rye each name their own module -- and a name match calls all four copies. A Rye module opens with a line naming its own path, so a file declaring somebody else's path is a copy by its own testimony.
think My first draft ran 23s. Reading symlink modes out of the git index (mode 120000) rather than stat-ing fourteen thousand paths, and one awk pass over 1,707 Rye heads rather than a head process apiece, brought it to 4s over the same answer.
obs My own draft carried the lap's lesson. IFS='\t' in POSIX sh is a literal backslash and a t rather than a tab, so the copy reading silently read zero -- and the reading that named it was the control's copy_seen leg, which is the whole argument for planting a fault and watching the guard speak.
obs The finding is %536's shape seven hours on, in a second room and found apart: there a duplicate answered "do the numbers cover 1..N" exactly as well as a unique row did; here a present file answered "is this a symlink" exactly as well as a symlink did. Two properties, one guard, and the guard held the easier one.
obs It is also DIFFUSER's morning finding one lane over -- six of eight map rows under-naming their guard, every gap running one way. Two ships measured the same asymmetry in different instruments on the same day without either reading the other, which is worth more than one measurement twice.
obs Left in Sound's room rather than taken: caravan/parse_int.rye. A symlink swap is behavior-identical and would let copy_lag's ceiling fall from 2 to 1, and reaching into a peer's room to lower a ceiling they set yesterday is a move to name rather than to make.
